{"Title":"An Act relative to the retirement of MassPort officers","BillNumber":"S1704","DocketNumber":"SD1497","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T15:26:13.91"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T15:26:13.91"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1704/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Moore, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1704) of Michael O. Moore for legislation relative to the retirement of MassPort officers.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 3 of chapter 32 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is amended in line by inserting after the word “men”, the second time it appears, in line 295, the following words:- \r\n\t; employees of the Massachusetts Port Authority who are employed as port officers and supervisors of said employees who shall include port sergeants, lieutenants, captains, assistant chiefs, deputy chiefs and directors.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}